<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1000"><title>Disable PAIR valve</title><description>Normal and diagnostic air-induction commands. Enabled means firmware control is available, not that the valve is currently open. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x9D5A" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="4DF002" basedata="4CF002"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0xBAC3" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="4DF002" basedata="4CF002"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1001"><title>Disable Immobilizer</title><description>Authentication configuration read by startup and runtime code. Detected from the bytes, including existing immobilizer-off BINs. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x4E7D" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="80" basedata="00"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1002"><title>Disable Overrun cut</title><description>Disabling bypasses the overrun routine and restores its normal fuel multiplier. Sensor thresholds, shared throttle state and rev-limit cuts remain unchanged. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x348A" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="90" basedata="90"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x765D" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="06777A" basedata="F608F4"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 3" address="0x778D" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="0677A2" basedata="F60900"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1003"><title>Disable Sidestand cut-off</title><description>Disabling allows the ECU to run with the stand down and suppresses new fault 19. The external starter-relay interlock still applies. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x4E6C" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="80" basedata="00"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0xCC5E" datasize="0x0004" patchdata="1D088C80" basedata="1C088C80"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1004"><title>Disable Lean-angle cut-off</title><description>Disabling removes ECU tip-over detection and the sensor fault-41 path: the engine may keep running after a fall. Existing latches or stored faults can still inhibit starting. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x4E91" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="80" basedata="00"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1005"><title>CO full-range override</title><description>Keeps dashboard CO correction at full strength across the running range. Apply = override enabled; Remove = stock fade-out. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x34B0" datasize="0x0015" patchdata="14001C000080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF" basedata="14001C000080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0000"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x800C" datasize="0x0025" patchdata="CE34B0FC090016C1F27A09A01E0A16020BF609FC1686237A095C2009F60A001686237A095D" basedata="CE34B0FC090016C1F27A09A01E0A16020BF609FC1686237A095C2009F60A001686237A095D"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 3" address="0x8623" datasize="0x002B" patchdata="C0802419CB8086801816F609A012C30080180E8680181624118600200DB609A012C300808B80240286FF3D" basedata="C0802419CB8086801816F609A012C30080180E8680181624118600200DB609A012C300808B80240286FF3D"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 4" address="0xD0F5" datasize="0x000A" patchdata="B60AED7A09FC1C088F80" basedata="B60AED7A09FC1C088F80"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1006"><title>Speedo disable</title><description>Apply one speed patch at a time; Remove it before selecting another. Zero remains zero; output is clamped to 0–255 pulses per reply. This changes dashboard speed and distance reporting only. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x4FA6" datasize="0x0018" patchdata="398600383DFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF565353011400FFFF" basedata="FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x6341" datasize="0x0006" patchdata="164FA67A08A7" basedata="B60AE37A08A7"/></XDFPATCH>
